INT. HOLLOW WHALE-BONE MARKET - NIGHT

A cathedral of ribs. Moonlight slants between them. Stalls of glass beads, herbs, bottled lightning. Torches burn blue.

ELDRIN, 40s, a gaunt wizard in a cloak stitched with eyes, stalks between stalls. SYLVETTE, 30s, a thief in a green hood, trails him by three paces. GORRAK, 50s, a troll in a leather apron, hauls a barrel. THISTLE, 10, a barefoot child with a lantern, skips ahead.

ELDRIN
(to everyone)
Hold your wares! The market is closing!

He lifts his staff. Eyes on his cloak snap open, scanning the stalls.

SYLVETTE
(muttering)
Closing. He says closing like it means something.

She slips a vial from a stall and into her sleeve. He doesn't turn.

He stops at a stall. Taps a jar of black powder.

ELDRIN
This. How much?

GORRAK
For him? Ten crowns.

ELDRIN
For whom?

GORRAK
For whoever asks.

ELDRIN
(to himself)
Everyone asks.

He drops coins into a bowl. Takes the jar. Holds it up to a torch. It glows. Behind him, Thistle tugs at Gorrak's apron.

THISTLE
Is that a dragon's tooth?

GORRAK
It's a very old tooth.

THISTLE
Can I touch it?

GORRAK
No.

She does. Sparks leap from her fingertips. She yelps, grinning.

SYLVETTE
(to Thistle, low)
Give that here.

THISTLE
It's mine.

SYLVETTE
It's his.

THISTLE
He gave it to me.

SYLVETTE
He doesn't give anything to anyone.

Eldrin turns. His eyes, on the cloak, all swivel to Sylvette. His real eyes stay on Thistle.

ELDRIN
(to Thistle)
Keep it.

THISTLE
Truly?

ELDRIN
(to Sylvette)
And you may keep the vial.

Sylvette stops cold. Slowly takes the vial from her sleeve.

SYLVETTE
How long have you known?

ELDRIN
Since you took it.

He turns away. The blue torches gutter. High above, between the ribs, a pale shape moves against the moon. A vast wing. A slow breath.

GORRAK
(to the whole market)
Everybody down.

The market goes still.

THISTLE
(whispering)
Is it the whale?

ELDRIN
It is the whale's dream.

He lowers his staff. The shape passes. The moonlight returns. Somewhere a bead rolls off a stall and clinks.
